module

public import CompositionAlgebras.Composition.NormClassification
public import CompositionAlgebras.Composition.Reduced.Splitness

/-!
# Automorphisms are the unital norm equivalences (`GPR 23.4`)

A **unital norm equivalence** of conic algebras is a linear equivalence carrying `1` to `1` and the
norm to the norm; `Composition/NormClassification.lean` produces them from arbitrary norm
isometries (`GPR 23.3`) and shows they preserve trace, conjugation and squares (`GPR 23.2`).

`GPR 23.4` compares them with algebra isomorphisms in the two directions that are true.

**(a) Every isomorphism or anti-isomorphism is a unital norm equivalence, in every rank.** The
norm of a finitely generated projective conic algebra is intrinsic (`GPR 16.16`), so a unital
linear equivalence preserving squares has no choice but to preserve it. This is
`ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_linearEquiv` for isomorphisms and
`ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_linearEquiv_of_map_mul_rev` for anti-isomorphisms, recorded here for a
self-map as `ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_automorphism`.

**(b) In rank two the converse holds.** Multiplication in a conic algebra generated by `1` and one
element `u` has only the two structure constants `t(u)` and `n(u)` (`GPR 19.8`), and a unital norm
equivalence preserves both; so it is automatically multiplicative. The hypothesis that the algebra
*is* `k[u]` is supplied in constant rank two by `GPR 19.16(b)` together with the exhaustion
criterion: the subalgebra `k[u]` produced there is regular of rank two, hence all of `A`.

⚠ `GPR 23.4(b)` is stated for every quadratic algebra over every commutative ring; its proof
localizes, where a generator exists. Here the generator is **global**: the general engine assumes
`A = k[u]`, and the composition-algebra statements obtain `u` over a nontrivial LG ring. The
localization argument for a quadratic algebra with no global generator is not formalized.

⚠ **(b) is false in higher rank**, which is why `GPR 23.4` is stated as it is. The standard
conjugation of a quaternion algebra is a unital norm equivalence — `ConicAlgebra.norm_conj` and
`ConicAlgebra.conj_one` — but it is an anti-automorphism, and a quaternion algebra is not
commutative (`ConicAlgebra.exists_mul_ne_mul_realQuaternion`). What rank two supplies is a property
of the algebra, not of the map.

## Main results

* `ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_automorphism` : **`GPR 23.4(a)`**.
* `ConicAlgebra.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement` : the engine of
  **`GPR 23.4(b)`** — a unital norm equivalence out of a monogenic conic algebra is multiplicative,
  over any commutative ring and with no regularity hypothesis.
* `ConicAlgebra.IsComposition.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two` :
  **`GPR 23.4(b)`** over a nontrivial LG ring, in constant rank two.
* `ConicAlgebra.IsComposition.map_mul_iff_norm_map_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two` : **`GPR 23.4`**, both
  directions at once: for a unital linear self-equivalence of a constant-rank-two composition
  algebra over a nontrivial LG ring, being an automorphism is equivalent to preserving the norm.
* `ConicAlgebra.IsComposition.isomorphic_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_finrank_eq_two` : the field
  case, which is the form `GPR` applies inside the Cayley–Dickson doubling arguments.

## Implementation notes

Since mathlib's `AlgEquiv` requires associative multiplication, an automorphism is expressed
throughout as a `LinearEquiv` together with `map_one` and `map_mul`, exactly as in
`Composition/NormClassification.lean` and `Composition/Reduced/Splitness.lean`. No new predicate is
introduced.

## References

* [GPR] Garibaldi, Petersson, Racine, *Albert Algebras over Commutative Rings*, 16.7, 19.3, 19.8,
  19.11, 19.16(b), 23.2--23.5.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

namespace ConicAlgebra

variable {k : Type u} {A : Type v} [CommRing k] [NonAssocRing A] [Module k A]
  [SMulCommClass k A A] [IsScalarTower k A A] [Module.Finite k A] [Module.Projective k A]
  {B : Type w} [NonAssocRing B] [Module k B] [SMulCommClass k B B] [IsScalarTower k B B]
  [Module.Finite k B] [Module.Projective k B]
  {C : ConicAlgebra k A} {D : ConicAlgebra k B}

/-! ### `GPR 23.4(a)`: isomorphisms are unital norm equivalences -/

omit [SMulCommClass k A A] [IsScalarTower k A A] in
/-- **`GPR 23.4(a)`.** Every automorphism of a finitely generated projective conic algebra is a
unital norm equivalence: it preserves the norm, and hence the trace and the conjugation.

This is the self-map case of `ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_linearEquiv`, and it holds in every rank
and over every commutative ring, because the conic norm on such an algebra is intrinsic
(`GPR 16.7`, `GPR 19.3`). -/
theorem norm_map_of_automorphism (C : ConicAlgebra k A) (e : A ≃ₗ[k] A)
    (map_one : e (1 : A) = 1) (map_mul : ∀ x y, e (x * y) = e x * e y) (x : A) :
    C.norm (e x) = C.norm x :=
  norm_map_of_linearEquiv C C e map_one map_mul x

/-! ### `GPR 23.4(b)`: in the monogenic case, unital norm equivalences are multiplicative -/

omit [Module.Finite k A] [Module.Projective k A] [Module.Finite k B] [Module.Projective k B] in
/-- **The engine of `GPR 23.4(b)`.** If every element of `A` lies in the quadratic subalgebra
`k[u]`, then every unital norm isometry out of `C` is multiplicative.

Multiplication in `k[u]` is the coefficient formula of `GPR 19.8`, whose only structure constants
are `t(u)` and `n(u)`; a unital norm isometry preserves the norm by hypothesis and the trace by
`GPR 23.2`, so it transports the formula. No regularity, projectivity, rank or characteristic
hypothesis is used. -/
theorem map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement (C : ConicAlgebra k A)
    (D : ConicAlgebra k B) (e : C.norm.IsometryEquiv D.norm) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) {u : A}
    (hu : ∀ x : A, x ∈ C.adjoinElement u) (x y : A) : e (x * y) = e x * e y := by
  have h := adjoinElementLinearEquivOfIsometryEquiv_map_mul C D e h1 u ⟨x, hu x⟩ ⟨y, hu y⟩
  exact congrArg (fun z : D.adjoinElement (e u) ↦ (z : B)) h

omit [Module.Finite k A] [Module.Projective k A] [Module.Finite k B] [Module.Projective k B] in
/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)`, as an isomorphism of conic algebras.** A unital norm isometry out of a
monogenic conic algebra is an isomorphism in the sense of `ConicAlgebra.Isomorphic`. -/
theorem isomorphic_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement (C : ConicAlgebra k A)
    (D : ConicAlgebra k B) (e : C.norm.IsometryEquiv D.norm) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) {u : A}
    (hu : ∀ x : A, x ∈ C.adjoinElement u) : C.Isomorphic D :=
  ⟨e, h1, map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement C D e h1 hu⟩

/-! ### Constant rank two -/

/-- A composition algebra of constant rank two over an LG ring is monogenic: the regular quadratic
subalgebra `k[u]` of `GPR 19.16(b)` has rank two as well, so the exhaustion criterion makes it the
whole algebra. -/
theorem IsComposition.exists_forall_mem_adjoinElement_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two [Nontrivial k]
    (hC : C.IsComposition.{u, v, u}) (hLG : IsLGRing k)
    (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2) :
    ∃ u : A, ∀ x : A, x ∈ C.adjoinElement u := by
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hC.exists_isRegularRankTwoComposition_of_rankAtStalk hLG (by
    intro 𝔭
    simp only [hA]
    omega)
  have hdisc : IsUnit (C.elementDiscriminant u) :=
    (C.isRegularRankTwoComposition_iff_isUnit_discriminant u).mp hu
  have hreg : QuadraticForm.IsGPRRegular (C.restrict (C.adjoinElement u)).norm :=
    C.normAdjoinElement_isGPRRegular hdisc
  have hrank : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k)
      (C.adjoinElement u).toNonUnitalSubalgebra.toSubmodule = fun _ ↦ 2 := by
    rw [rankAtStalk_toSubmodule, ← Module.rankAtStalk_eq_of_equiv (C.quadraticSpanEquiv hdisc),
      Module.rankAtStalk_prod, Module.rankAtStalk_self]
    rfl
  exact ⟨u, fun x ↦ mem_of_isGPRRegular_of_rankAtStalk_eq hreg hA hrank x⟩

omit [Module.Finite k B] [Module.Projective k B] in
/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)`.** Over a nontrivial LG ring, every unital norm isometry out of a
constant-rank-two composition algebra is multiplicative. -/
theorem IsComposition.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two [Nontrivial k]
    (hC : C.IsComposition.{u, v, u}) (hLG : IsLGRing k)
    (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2) (e : C.norm.IsometryEquiv D.norm)
    (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) (x y : A) : e (x * y) = e x * e y := by
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hC.exists_forall_mem_adjoinElement_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two hLG hA
  exact map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement C D e h1 hu x y

omit [Module.Finite k B] [Module.Projective k B] in
/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)`, as an isomorphism.** Over a nontrivial LG ring, a unital norm isometry between
composition algebras of constant rank two is an isomorphism of conic algebras. -/
theorem IsComposition.isomorphic_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two [Nontrivial k]
    (hC : C.IsComposition.{u, v, u}) (hLG : IsLGRing k)
    (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2) (e : C.norm.IsometryEquiv D.norm)
    (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) : C.Isomorphic D :=
  ⟨e, h1, hC.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two hLG hA e h1⟩

/-- **`GPR 23.4`, both directions.** Let `C` be a composition algebra of constant rank two over a
nontrivial LG ring and let `e` be a linear self-equivalence of `A` fixing `1`. Then `e` is an
algebra automorphism if and only if it preserves the norm.

Forwards is `GPR 23.4(a)` and holds in every rank; backwards is `GPR 23.4(b)` and is where rank two
is used. -/
theorem IsComposition.map_mul_iff_norm_map_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two [Nontrivial k]
    (hC : C.IsComposition.{u, v, u}) (hLG : IsLGRing k)
    (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2) (e : A ≃ₗ[k] A) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) :
    (∀ x y, e (x * y) = e x * e y) ↔ ∀ x, C.norm (e x) = C.norm x := by
  constructor
  · intro hmul x
    exact norm_map_of_automorphism C e h1 hmul x
  · intro hnorm
    exact hC.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two hLG hA
      { toLinearEquiv := e, map_app' := hnorm } h1

/-! ### The field case -/

section Field

variable {K : Type u} {X : Type v} {Y : Type w} [Field K]
  [NonAssocRing X] [Module K X] [SMulCommClass K X X] [IsScalarTower K X X]
  [Module.Finite K X] [Module.Projective K X]
  [NonAssocRing Y] [Module K Y] [SMulCommClass K Y Y] [IsScalarTower K Y Y]
  [Module.Finite K Y] [Module.Projective K Y]
  {E : ConicAlgebra K X} {F : ConicAlgebra K Y}

omit [Module.Finite K Y] [Module.Projective K Y] in
/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)` over a field.** A unital norm isometry out of a two-dimensional composition
algebra over a field is multiplicative. This is the form used inside the Cayley–Dickson doubling
arguments, where the quadratic étale subalgebra of a quaternion algebra is compared with itself. -/
theorem IsComposition.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_finrank_eq_two
    (hE : E.IsComposition.{u, v, u}) (hX : Module.finrank K X = 2)
    (e : E.norm.IsometryEquiv F.norm) (h1 : e (1 : X) = 1) (x y : X) :
    e (x * y) = e x * e y :=
  hE.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two (isLGRing_of_field K)
    (Module.rankAtStalk_eq_of_finrank_eq hX) e h1 x y

omit [Module.Finite K Y] [Module.Projective K Y] in
/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)` over a field, as an isomorphism.** -/
theorem IsComposition.isomorphic_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_finrank_eq_two
    (hE : E.IsComposition.{u, v, u}) (hX : Module.finrank K X = 2)
    (e : E.norm.IsometryEquiv F.norm) (h1 : e (1 : X) = 1) : E.Isomorphic F :=
  ⟨e, h1, hE.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_finrank_eq_two hX e h1⟩

/-- **`GPR 23.4` over a field, both directions.** For a unital linear self-equivalence of a
two-dimensional composition algebra over a field, being an automorphism is the same as preserving
the norm. -/
theorem IsComposition.map_mul_iff_norm_map_of_finrank_eq_two (hE : E.IsComposition.{u, v, u})
    (hX : Module.finrank K X = 2) (e : X ≃ₗ[K] X) (h1 : e (1 : X) = 1) :
    (∀ x y, e (x * y) = e x * e y) ↔ ∀ x, E.norm (e x) = E.norm x :=
  hE.map_mul_iff_norm_map_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two (isLGRing_of_field K)
    (Module.rankAtStalk_eq_of_finrank_eq hX) e h1

end Field

end ConicAlgebra
